{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1481887-what-sort-of-fan-supplement-would-demon-fans-like-to-see","id":1481887,"title":"What sort of fan supplement would Demon fans like to see?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-05-24T18:26:56-07:00","id":1481887,"title":"What sort of fan supplement would Demon fans like to see?","content":"One thing that always ground my gears was how Demon had so few supplements. I was thinking of using a little time here and there, later in my semester to try and write a fan supplement. <br /> <br /> Maybe a sidekick and adversaries book for Demons? Like going into more depth about the sort of creatures that they can now summon, create, or have discovered hiding since before the Fall? I am particularly thinking of plasmids, either natural or constructed, who have been imbued with a few tricks. <br /> <br /> And maybe also a new, modern Lore for interacting with the Middle Umbra and commanding its denizens. I don\u2019t know if I\u2019ll have the time, since I need indirect hours to sit for my exam, but if I do find the time, is there anything the Demon fans might want to see?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-24T22:35:58-07:00","id":1481897,"title":"","content":"A Hunter like Antagonist/protagonist? group would be nice, where you play the agent of the Host, or an Angel itself, to clear the fog, what the hell happened with the Elohim, what is the Second World, what exactly was the Ophanim who judged the Sebettu after their defeat, and what was the Malhim exactly and their fate (eg. Ziana, the Seraph of the Cycle, ruler of the Sixth House of angels was/is really Gaia/The Scarlet Queen/Phoenix? The nwho is the Ebon Dragon? Whats whit the Wan Xian and the Messangers of the Hunters? The Fera are really the descendants of the Malhim?) Whats happened with Michael and where is he now? Michael, Lucifer sucessor as the leader of the Angels led the final charge in the War of Heaven at Genhinnom that resulted in Heaven's victory and the banishment of the Fallen to the Abyss. Rumors are that before the night of banishment, Michael went to the chained Lucifer. What they talked about is unknown, but afterwards, the seraph threw away his sword and left it within Creation...<br /> What was the Host original Lore-spread? Several of the Sebettu Lore were &quot;made&quot; after the Fall and was unkwnon to the Host. For example originally, the Annunaki had only two forms. The Kishar created the Earth and everything upon it, save for life. The Antu made movement and travel upon the Kishar's creation possible. After the fall, the Malefactors were determined to help humans survive. Toguiel offered to create tools and shelter for Adam and Eve, but they were determined to create things themselves. While constructing a house of stones, Adam had difficulty in moving one large rock, and so one of the Malefactors created the lever to help him. In teaching mankind how to create and use tools, a new visage, the Mummu, were created and the Lore of the Forge with it, but the same goes for the Namaru. A new kind of Namaru, the Qingu, appeared shortly after the Fall to inspire humans to new heights of greatness and obedience along with the Lore of Radiance...<br /> The Time of Judgement gives a little help, such a characters, but a bit endgame scenarios...<br /> What is the realtion of the Angels with the Salubri? The Salubri warriors with the Blooding Ritual takes up the Celestial Name of an Angel... and several of their power is fuelled by thei power... the angel must exist to share it power (with an undead, cursed by THEM... ouch)<br /> Would be nice to know the &quot;details and truths&quot;<br /> <br /> A supplement focusing on the Nephilim and their fate would be nice too<br /> Considering Lucifer was a bit hypocrit when it came to them, since he had a nice little affair with Lilith a technically Human and had children of their own with her... but according Houses of the Fallen, it was a relic that allowed a Fallen to have a child with a mortal and the Annunaki (Zipacna?) who made it just escaped from the Abyss....<br /> Azrael was the only one not involved with the creation of the Nephilim to discover their origin. He traded his silence, and the aid of the Alabaster Legion in rebellion against Lucifer, for the right to their souls when they finally passed on. These dead Nephilim worked as ferrymen in Haven, a job which was made easier due to their dual nature. What has happened to these dead Nephilim is unknow... did they really became the OG Ferryman and shaped Writh society? We know (more or less) Azrael's greatest and last fortress eventually became the Labyrinth and several of his underlings went missing... did the became the Malfeans of the Lebyrinth? Not to mention, many demons wonder if any of the supernaturals that populate the modern world are descendants of the ancient Nephilim.or not?<br /> <br /> Lets throw a curve Ball, the Mokol\u00e9 and their Mnesis goes back to the Age of the Kings, millions of years back, with their own civilization... Humanity actually Creation 2.0? Or even the whole &quot;curent&quot; Host are actually a new breed of Angels, when the first try with the lizard folks colapsed... and they tried the mammalian route? (inspired by the raptor jesus meme... reptilian Angels? Siting on their scally behind in Haven a bit morose they failed... but with a sinister a bit gleefull smile when the Fall happened, waiting their time to return)<br /> <br /> My list is basically endless","signature":"","edited":{"userid":23890,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","user":"Shadeprowler","date":". 05-25-2022, 01:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23890-shadeprowler","name":"Shadeprowler","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23890_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"928"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-25T10:25:46-07:00","id":1481933,"title":"","content":"Between Heaven and Hell, a book on Demon cosmology. Not only could we see how the Fallen view the current state of the Umbra, but also glimpse of the &quot;pocket spaces&quot; left over from the wars. Also, systems for locating old ones and building entire new ones, how other supernaturals interact with such spaces, and maybe even a brief look into the Halls of Creation before the wars.<br /> As a counterpoint, a more interactive system for running Angels (perhaps, Angel: The Message?) in the modern day. I have been trying to create systems for how such beings would work, without, say, possessing the bodies of the recently dead. Maybe creating a whole new physical form out of the 'dust' as it were, but having to relearn all of their old powers back slowly. All the time, facing the dangers of becoming too used to the modern world and the weaknesses of the flesh (Ennui instead of Torment), as well as the possibility that they might never return to the Halls of Creation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>THWarted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/17984-toby-weingarten","name":"Toby Weingarten","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"112"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-25T10:57:56-07:00","id":1481936,"title":"","content":"It's honestly about time for a 20th Anniversary Edition, not that such a thing would get through development process in time. If you cut out all the short fiction, you could squeeze updated versions of the crunch from every published D:tF book into one volume.<br /> <br /> I'd have loved to see a rebalancing of the seven houses' Lore and Apocalyptic Form powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-25T10:59:27-07:00","id":1481938,"title":"","content":"A fan errata on updates to the mechanics perhaps? It doesn't seem like we're getting a DTF20, so a translation guide/fan errata that cleaned up the broken and inconsistent powers would be nice.<br /> <br /> For example: how high torment lores seem to be kind of all over the place. Some lores are more powerful at high torment, some are useless. It's like the writers couldn't decide if they wanted High Torment to be a straight punishment or if using the evil magic was supposed to be tempting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reasor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1481887-what-sort-of-fan-supplement-would-demon-fans-like-to-see?p=1481936#post1481936\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd have loved to see a rebalancing of the seven houses' Lore and Apocalyptic Form powers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Personally made several attempts at trying to make a &quot;best of both worlds&quot; system between DTF modern and Devil's Due, but always run into the issue that getting lores and an apocalyptic form builder on the same being is a Messy system that's a Nightmare to balance.<br /> <br /> It's hard to make a range of options for apocalyptic forms with out stepping on the toes of lores when the 23 lores have 2 sets of powers at each level(plus 3 earthbound lores) because of torment shenanigans. :'(","signature":"","edited":{"userid":6383,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","user":"Prometheas","date":". 05-25-2022, 02:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-27T12:56:21-07:00","id":1482095,"title":"","content":"I'd be interested in a Nephilim supplement because:<br /> <br /> a.) I thought the Lucifuge concept was really interesting in Hunter the Vigil and having a a group of awakened beings who fit a similar mold (but not necessarily all hunters) would be interesting.<br /> <br /> b.) It would be interesting to see how one rationalized Nephilim compared to other awakened beings. Are they like the Imbued (or old pseudo-Exalted types like the Wan Kuei) or are they perhaps variations on the undead and/or mortal/spirit analogues we have like Garou, Changelings, and the like? Or do they manifest as something like a mage? Or maybe all of the above? There's alot of ways one could go about that depending on the direction one wanted to go with the lore, and it would be interesting to explore. <br /> <br /> <br /> I'd also like to see more development of the Elohim and that side of things (what happened to them) and their relation to other equally spiritual beings (Messengers, Psychopomps, Banes, what have you.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25533-mister_dunpeal","name":"Mister_Dunpeal","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25533_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"308"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-27T19:41:14-07:00","id":1482121,"title":"","content":"I think the Djinn would make good Nephilim. They even (might) have the potential to Awaken.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-27T21:01:55-07:00","id":1482126,"title":"","content":"The Nephilim go down in D:tF's fictional history as the worst idea the Fallen ever had, in a story that begins, ends, and is packed in the middle with them having bad ideas. It would probably be an utter disaster if they were to return.<br /> <br /> I like to think that the angels loyal to Heaven simply went back to doing their jobs after the war was over. There's absolutely nothing that suggests that, except that stars are still born, the planets still turn, life still evolves, and things still die to make room for the next generation. This was what the Elohim were all supposed to be doing before a third of them fell. Maybe nobody can see the rest because they're not revealing themselves, as ordered. The plan is still in place, and all is working as it was meant to be. It's a weird idea to fit into the World of Darkness, but that's part of its charm for me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-27T21:21:29-07:00","id":1482128,"title":"","content":"I like the Nephilim, but only as ghosts for any games I might want to play. And even then, they exist only VERY deep in the Labyrinth.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-28T07:39:09-07:00","id":1482156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reasor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1481887-what-sort-of-fan-supplement-would-demon-fans-like-to-see?p=1482126#post1482126\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like to think that the angels loyal to Heaven simply went back to doing their jobs after the war was over. There's absolutely nothing that suggests that, except that stars are still born, the planets still turn, life still evolves, and things still die to make room for the next generation. This was what the Elohim were all supposed to be doing before a third of them fell. Maybe nobody can see the rest because they're not revealing themselves, as ordered. The plan is still in place, and all is working as it was meant to be. It's a weird idea to fit into the World of Darkness, but that's part of its charm for me.</div> </div> </div> </div>That also fits with the idea suggested in ToJ that The Fall and the current state of WoD was completely intended and part of the plan.<br /> <br /> <i>Really</i> re-contextualizes the scene where Lucifer gets sniped by a &quot;blessed&quot; hunter and the bullet turns out to be carrying a message from god telling them to seek forgiveness. &quot;Come forth and repent your sins... For doing Exactly what I ordered you to do in Exactly the way I intended it&quot;(and Lucifer's reaction becomes infinitely more hilarious in context).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-28T11:47:03-07:00","id":1482183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Reasor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1481887-what-sort-of-fan-supplement-would-demon-fans-like-to-see?p=1482126#post1482126\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Nephilim go down in D:tF's fictional history as the worst idea the Fallen ever had, in a story that begins, ends, and is packed in the middle with them having bad ideas. It would probably be an utter disaster if they were to return.<br /> <br /> I like to think that the angels loyal to Heaven simply went back to doing their jobs after the war was over. There's absolutely nothing that suggests that, except that stars are still born, the planets still turn, life still evolves, and things still die to make room for the next generation. This was what the Elohim were all supposed to be doing before a third of them fell. Maybe nobody can see the rest because they're not revealing themselves, as ordered. The plan is still in place, and all is working as it was meant to be. It's a weird idea to fit into the World of Darkness, but that's part of its charm for me.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think this is a cool idea. But I am also fond of the idea that the Creator has turned his eyes from Earth and the Imbued are being created by renegade angels.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/986-mercurial","name":"Mercurial","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar986_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-05-28T12:47:50-07:00","id":1482187,"title":"","content":"The unreliability of Fallen's narrators provides rich potential for Storytellers to work with. These cocky creatures who thought they could second-guess God step out of the Abyss, having missed out on so much of the history of the universe that they're surrounded by tantalizing mysteries to explore and gaps for you to fill in. I think it's one of the setting's strengths. You can make so many different things out of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}